# reweight card for example 08: one sample generated at c8q2W2Dx1 = 1, reweighted to other points.
# Each "launch" block defines a new weight; parameters not listed keep the generation values.
#
# It used to vary c8W2H2D2x1, which is class 7 and has no diagram in p p > w+ w- at all, so the
# sample was the Standard Model and four of the five weights were degenerate with it and with
# each other.  c8q2W2Dx1 is the largest single-operator interference in that process, -1.189 pb.
change rwgt_dir rwgt
launch --rwgt_name=c8q2W2Dx1_0
  set c8q2W2Dx1 0.0
launch --rwgt_name=c8q2W2Dx1_m1
  set c8q2W2Dx1 -1.0
launch --rwgt_name=c8q2W2Dx1_2
  set c8q2W2Dx1 2.0
launch --rwgt_name=c8q2WH2Dx1_1
  set c8q2W2Dx1 0.0
  set c8q2WH2Dx1 1.0
launch --rwgt_name=Lam_2TeV
# "set Lam 2000" is silently ignored: MadGraph lowercases the name, the Standard Model already
# has a "lam", and the written card therefore calls the scale lam__2.  Address it by block and id.
  set dim8 0 2000
